summary: Configure kdump_pre/kdump_post option.
description: |+
    It allows to run a cmd in kdump_pre or kdump_post script. The result of cmd
    can be output to sysroot and verified in a later step.

    Parameters

    - TESTARGS: the command will be run in kdump_pre or kdump_post script

    - OPTION: kdump_pre or kdump_post. Only these 2 option are allowed.

    - OUTPUT_TO_ROOT: Whether you cmd will save result to sys root (/mnt/tmproot in
        2n kernel). e.g. TESTARGS="dmesg > /mnt/tmproot/2nd-kernel-dmesg.txt"
        If yes, sysroot will be mounted explicitly to /mnt/tmproot in 2n kernel.
        Only 'true' or 'false' is allowed. By default it's 'ture'.

    Note,
        kdump initrd img contains minimum set of binaries and modules.
        If you'd like to run some special commands or modules. Make sure they are
        added through extra_bins or extra_modules by kernel/kdump/config-any test.


        Since RHEL-7.5, kdump won't mount /sysroot by default if dump target is a
        non-root target and 'default dump_to_rootfs' is not specified in kdump.conf.
        If you'd like to mount root in your script, and you root file system is
        xfs. Make sure "extra_modules xfs" is set in /etc/kdump.conf

contact: Kdump QE <kdump-qe-list@redhat.com>
test: chmod a+x ./runtest.sh; ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
require:
  - kexec-tools
duration: 10m
extra-summary: /kernel/kdump/config-script
extra-task: /kernel/kdump/config-script
